research/A07_JOBS.md:49:- `avgpcon` (also `minpcon`, `maxpcon`): W. The feature list calls it "Average node power consuption", but the paper states "The power consumption is the sum of the minimum, average, or maximum power consumption of the resources allocated to the job during its execution", and `econ = avgpcon * duration / 3600` with no node factor, so it is a whole-job power. Median `power_w / nodes` is about 93 to 102 W per node in five of six node-count bins (47.6 W in the 17 to 64 node bin; the cause was not investigated, possibly allocated nodes above used nodes, since 21_04 has jobs with `nnuma` 12 and `nnumu` 1); therefore `power_w` = `avgpcon` as is, `energy_kwh` = `econ` / 1000 (measured). 
